 "observations": [
  "The page number «214» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the left the number of the table, «Tab. 99», in bold sans serif, underlined. The page has no signature and no title: the folios of the manuscripts stand at the left above the double rule of the first field, in two lines of their own, «C 94v, O 150r,» and «N 61r.», the second indented, the letters raised (L01-L02).",
  "The page holds three fields, as pp. 206-213 (JP2 0238-0245): «Quinque1) gradus Leonis» (L03), «Decem2) gradus Leonis» (L15) and «Quindecim3) gradus Leonis» (L23), the ascendant at 5°, 10° and 15° of Leo, with the numbers for the sextile, the quadrature and the trine (L04, L16, L24); headings and numbers in bold. The columns begin with the sign of the ascendant: «Leo Aquarius Horoscopus», «Virgo Pisces Horoscopus», «Libra Aries Horoscopus», «Scorpius Taurus Horoscopus», «Sagittar. Gemini Horoscopus» and «Capricorn. Cancer Horoscopus», without notes; here each head is set from the top, one printed line to a line (L05-L07), with «Gradus aequales», printed upwards, in L05-L06, and the units in L08. The numbers are counted from the beginning of Leo. The second and the third field have no heads. Double rules divide the fields. The long dash after the note e in L16 is made up of two short dashes (18 and 17 px with a gap of 4 px); here written as two hyphens (U+2010).",
  "The numbers at the head of a field, as on pp. 206-212 (JP2 0238-0244), are a third, a half and two thirds of the last number of the field: 199° 18′ (L14) gives 66° 26′, 99° 39′ and 132° 52′, as printed (L04); 201° 50′ (L22) gives 67° 16.7′, 100° 55′ and 134° 33.3′, printed 67° 17′, 100° 57′ and 134° 34′ (L16), the quadrature 2′ more; 203° 55′ (L30) gives 67° 58.3′, 101° 57.5′ and 135° 56.7′, printed 67° 58′, 101° 57′ and 135° 56′ (L24).",
  "The columns: in Leo the three fields lie within 15′ of the oblique ascensions from the beginning of Leo for the latitude 38° 30′ (computed with the obliquity 23° 35′; 6° 14′, 12° 31′, 18° 48′, 25° 6′, 31° 23′, 37° 39′), and in Virgo within 30′, 43′ and 22′, mostly below them; from Libra on they fall far below them, to 199° 18′, 201° 50′ and 203° 55′ at the end of Capricornus, where the oblique ascension from the beginning of Leo is 214° 10′. The column of Leo of the second field (L17-L22) is that of the first (L09-L14), number for number.",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the other fields, which differ by 5° of the ascendant, and by the steps of the columns: the edition's readings are the nearer in the quadrature of the first field (note a, L04: C's 99 against O's 96; half of 199° 18′ is 99° 39′), at 15° of Leo in the first (note b, L11: C's 0 against O's 5, the steps 6° 19′ and 6° 18′ against 6° 24′ and 6° 13′; 19° 0′ in the second field), at 20° of Capricornus in the first (note d, L12: the 187 of O and N against C's 186, the steps 5° 52′ and 6° 7′ against 4° 52′ and 7° 7′), in the sextile of the second (note e, L16: C's 17 against O's 18; a third of 201° 50′ is 67° 16.7′), at 15° of Virgo in the second (note f, L19: the editor's 56 for the 50 of all three manuscripts, between 49° 55′ and 62° 10′) and at 25° and 30° of Libra in the third (notes i and k, L29-L30: the editor's 12 and 17 for the 112 and 117 of the manuscripts, in the minutes). At 25° of Virgo in the first field (note c, L13) C's 38 gives the steps 5° 53′ and 5° 45′, the 28 of O and N 5° 43′ and 5° 55′; neither is decided.",
  "At 25° and 30° of Sagittarius in the second field (notes g and h, L21-L22) the 160 and 164 of O and N, which the edition adopts, are nearer than C's 140 and 144, but both lie below the course of the column: the steps are 4° 30′ and 3° 28′ and then 8° 20′ into Capricornus, where the other fields have 5° 25′, 5° 25′ and 5° 30′ (L12-L14, L09) and 5° 14′, 5° 28′ and 5° 22′ (L28-L30, L25), and the second field lies 1° 17′ above and 40′ below the first there, where it lies 2° 12′ to 2° 14′ above it from 5° to 20° of Sagittarius. With 161° 42′ and 167° 10′ the steps would be 5° 30′, 5° 28′ and 5° 20′. The apparatus has no reading that gives these numbers.",
  "In the first field the step from the end of Virgo to 5° of Libra is 4° 1′ (L14, L09), against 5° 18′ and 5° 40′ in the other fields (L22, L17; L30, L25), and that from 10° to 15° of Virgo 6° 58′ (L10-L11).",
  "The 6 of «56» at 15° of Virgo in the second field (L19) is broken: its upper stroke stands detached above the bowl, like a circumflex over an o. The i of «Min.» over Capricornus (L08) is blotted. Specks in the margins; not transcribed."
